- ✅ Test your implementations
- ✅ Use meaningful branch names

### **CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md - What to Know**

**Purpose:** Explains behavioral expectations for community participation

**Key principles typically include:**
- **Be respectful** - No harassment, discrimination, or trolling
- **Be constructive** - Criticize ideas, not people
- **Be inclusive** - Welcome newcomers, help others learn
- **Be professional** - Keep discussions on-topic and appropriate

**Why This Matters for GSOC:**
- Mentors want to work with people who are pleasant to collaborate with
- Community interaction is part of the evaluation
- Violations can lead to removal from the program

**When Interacting on Discord/GitHub:**
- ✅ Ask questions politely
- ✅ Thank people who help you
- ✅ Share your knowledge with others
- ✅ Be patient with responses
- ❌ Don't demand immediate answers
- ❌ Don't be rude if rejected
- ❌ Don't spam channels

